 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "routes is a list of [prefix, nextHop] where prefix is \"a.b.c.d/k\" (0 <= k <= 32; host bits of the base may be non-zero and are ignored) and queries a list of IPv4 addresses. For each query return the nextHop of the matching route with the longest prefix length; when several routes have the same prefix length and the same first k bits, the one listed last wins. Return \"\" for a query no route covers. Answers are in query order.",
  "provenance": [
